# Frontend Development Rules

## Code Style
- Functional React components with hooks — no class components
- TailwindCSS for ALL styling — no CSS files, no CSS-in-JS, no inline styles
- Zustand for state management — no Redux, no Context for global state
- TypeScript strict mode — no `any` types

## Component Patterns

### App Views
Each app (Dashboard, Files, Docker, etc.) follows this pattern:
```typescript
export function SomeView() {
  const { serverId } = useActiveServer();
  const [data, setData] = useState(null);
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);
  const [error, setError] = useState(null);

  // Fetch data from backend
  useEffect(() => { ... }, [serverId]);

  // Always handle all 3 states:
  if (loading) return <LoadingSpinner />;
  if (error) return <ErrorState message={error} onRetry={...} />;
  if (!data) return <EmptyState message="..." />;

  return <Table columns={columns} data={data} />;
}
```

### State Management (Zustand)
```typescript
// client/src/store/app-store.ts
interface AppState {
  servers: ServerConfig[];
  activeServerId: string | null;
  tabs: Tab[];
  activeTabId: string | null;
  terminalVisible: boolean;
  // ... actions
}
```

### Single-Instance Tabs
Some tabs (Terminal, Dashboard) only allow one instance per server:
```typescript
openTab: (app) => {
  const existing = get().tabs.find(t => t.appId === app.id && t.serverId === activeServerId);
  if (existing && app.singleInstance) {
    set({ activeTabId: existing.id });
    return;
  }
  // Create new tab...
}
```

## Security
- NEVER use `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` with terminal output
- Terminal output goes through xterm.js only (handles ANSI safely)
- All data comes from the backend — frontend never calls APIs directly to remote servers
- No frontend polling — backend handles poll intervals and caching

## UI Components
- Reusable primitives go in `client/src/components/ui/`
- App-specific components go in `client/src/components/{AppName}/`
- Use Lucide React for icons
- Dark theme via TailwindCSS dark mode
- Context menus for all data views (files, containers, processes)

## AppWindow (Modal Dialogs — MANDATORY)
**All overlay/dialog/window UI MUST use `AppWindow`** from `@/components/ui/app-window`.
See `docs/UI_DESIGN.md` for full design system reference.

Sizes: xs (380×260), sm (480×400), md (680×520), lg (900×620), xl (1100×720)

```tsx
<AppWindow open={open} onOpenChange={setOpen} title="Title" icon={Icon} size="lg">
  <AppWindow.Sidebar width={200}>
    <AppWindow.SidebarGroup label="Section">
      <AppWindow.SidebarItem id="x" icon={Icon} label="Label" active onClick={...} />
    </AppWindow.SidebarGroup>
  </AppWindow.Sidebar>
  <AppWindow.Toolbar>{/* actions */}</AppWindow.Toolbar>
  <AppWindow.Body>{/* content */}</AppWindow.Body>
  <AppWindow.Footer>{/* status */}</AppWindow.Footer>
</AppWindow>
```

Sidebar, Toolbar, Footer are optional. Use `noPadding` on Body for terminal/grids.

## File Locations
| Purpose | Path |
|---------|------|
| App entry | `client/src/App.tsx` |
| Layout | `client/src/components/Shell/` |
| Dashboard | `client/src/components/Dashboard/` |
| File Explorer | `client/src/components/FileExplorer/` |
| Docker | `client/src/components/Docker/` |
| Terminal | `client/src/components/Terminal/` |
| Reusable UI | `client/src/components/ui/` |
| State | `client/src/store/` |
| Hooks | `client/src/hooks/` |
| Shared types | `shared/types.ts` |
